Z||000000||CUTTER||08-26-99||12:53 AM||||Hey I raced a 91 or a 92 5.0 mustang with my almost stock 87GT fiero(flowmasters, holley throttle body)we raced from a side by side drag street race, 0-30 we were dead even, then he pulled ahead, around 70-80 he was about 2 fiero lengths ahead.....not bad for a almost stock 2.8fiero huh? also I killed a 3.1L camaro v6...they suck!!!!!
Z||000001||Shaun41178||08-26-99||01:26 AM||||Cutter, nice kill of the v6 camaro.  They have 160 hp but they weight over 3300 pounds so they are quite heavy.  I have kept up with my friends 305 TBI rated at 170 hp and 255 torque.  He only pulled a car up to 70 mph and that was before any of my mods!  I am sure I could take him now without my nitrous and I have already waxed him with my nitrous.  We both have auto trannys.<p>The holley throttle body is stock from the factory on all V6 Fieros.  That is not an aftermarket TB.  So I guess the only mod you have is the flowmaster muffler.  Still pretty good job with that mustang.  You have an auto or manual tranny?<p>A couple more mods and you should be able to take that mustang.  Later
Z||000002||CUTTER||08-26-99||01:38 AM||||I have a auto trans. I shift 1st to 2nd manually, then throw it to drive, I also line locked it before the race with the RUSTANG, do you think it is faster to shift 1 to 2nd manually or keep it in drive from the start?
Z||000003||CUTTER||08-26-99||01:57 AM||||If any of you care it was a 91 camaro RS 3.1 with t-tops. Past him at 120MPH and he said "the peddle was to the floor" 
